BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Navigating the Strait of Hormuz: Regional Peacemaking Amid the U.S
 .-Iran Conflict
DTSTART:20260701T180000Z
DTEND:20260701T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260701T073553Z
UID:8ad2ae74-550e-5116-bb7f-2f21eee57419
DESCRIPTION:With one-fifth of global oil supplies and the movement of crit
 ical LNG stuck in the crosshairs of a military standoff\, the need for dip
 lomatic off-ramps has never been more urgent. This panel brings together t
 op diplomats and geopolitical experts to unpack the overlapping mediation 
 efforts of key regional powers. From Pakistan’s frontline ceasefire nego
 tiations to Qatar’s high-stakes maneuvering over nuclear frameworks and 
 frozen assets\, and Oman’s delicate balancing act of historical neutrali
 ty.\n\nMore info & tickets: https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/2026-0
 7-01/navigating-strait-hormuz-regional-peacemaking-amid-us-iran-conflict
LOCATION:The Commonwealth Club of California\, Toni Rembe Rock Auditorium\
 , San Francisco\, CA
URL:https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/2026-07-01/navigating-strait-h
 ormuz-regional-peacemaking-amid-us-iran-conflict
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Humanities West presents the 250th Anniversary of the Declaration 
 of Independence
DTSTART:20260702T000000Z
DTEND:20260702T020000Z
DTSTAMP:20260701T073553Z
UID:a61c2ec5-6252-5332-a12f-7c6417f87245
DESCRIPTION:It has been 250 years since upstart young leaders of the Ameri
 can colonies declared independence from King George III and imagined found
 ing a republic\, based on a democracy of sorts\, which has\, over 25 decad
 es of difficult growth and adjustment\, arrived at our current version of 
 a government “of the people\, by the people\, for the people\,” as Pre
 sident Lincoln put it.\n\nMore info & tickets: https://www.commonwealthclu
 b.org/events/2026-07-01/humanities-west-presents-250th-anniversary-declara
 tion-independence
LOCATION:The Commonwealth Club of California\, Taube Family Auditorium\, S
 an Francisco\, CA
URL:https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/2026-07-01/humanities-west-pre
 sents-250th-anniversary-declaration-independence
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Imperfect Circles Discussion Group at the Orinda Library
DTSTART:20260703T013000Z
DTEND:20260703T033000Z
DTSTAMP:20260701T073553Z
UID:979c650d-2629-5b4f-95c9-7ac1edbe6a20
DESCRIPTION:Are you a person who never tires of talking or thinking about 
 philosophical\, scientific or religious theories? Are you interested in ps
 ychological insights\, or attempts at such insights\, into human life? The
 re are many who would insist that being realistic about human life means y
 ou should ignore such fundamental questions—starting around the time the
  ink dries on your diploma. But it is unrealistic to ignore the fundamenta
 l explanatory concepts that underlie each successful human civilization—
 concepts that sometimes help and sometimes hinder us in our pursuit of hap
 piness.\n\nMore info & tickets: https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/20
 26-07-02/imperfect-circles-discussion-group-orinda-library
LOCATION:Orinda Public Library\, 26 Orinda Way\, Orinda\, CA
URL:https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/2026-07-02/imperfect-circles-d
 iscussion-group-orinda-library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dr. Jennifer Grandis: Why Women Can’t Get Ahead in Science and H
 ealth Care
DTSTART:20260707T010000Z
DTEND:20260707T030000Z
DTSTAMP:20260701T073553Z
UID:31fd1272-654c-5b12-b306-b943d99110a8
DESCRIPTION:Women continue to face systemic barriers in medicine and scien
 ce\, despite decades of progress. What is happening?\nIn Harsh Medicine\, 
 Dr. Jennifer R. Grandis draws on decades of experience as a physician-scie
 ntist\, mentor and leader to expose how deeply gender bias is embedded in 
 the structures of academic medicine and scientific research. Through rigor
 ous analysis\, real-world case studies\, and personal insight\, she argues
  that policies\, funding systems\, promotion practices and cultural norms 
 continue to disadvantage women at every stage of their careers.\n\nMore in
 fo & tickets: https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/2026-07-06/dr-jennif
 er-grandis-why-women-cant-get-ahead-science-and-health-care
LOCATION:Commonwealth Club World Affairs of California\, Taube Family Audi
 torium\, San Francisco\, CA
URL:https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/2026-07-06/dr-jennifer-grandis
 -why-women-cant-get-ahead-science-and-health-care
END:VEVENT
